<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koreans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Koreans are the people of the Korean Peninsula, divided since 1945 between North and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, with large communities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Japan ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> from 1910 to 1945 and moved many Koreans as labourers. In 1937 Stalin deported the whole Korean population of the Soviet Far East to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/koreans.jpg" alt="Koreans" width="320" height="166" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Allice Hunter · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Korean_Diaspora_in_the_World.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
